      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To study the distribution of polymorphism of c.212-37insC (rs3832879) in intron 1 of fibroblast growth factor 23 (FGF23) gene and its association with Kawasaki disease (KD) and coronary artery lesions (CAL)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Forty children with KD were enrolled in this study, among whom 16 children had concurrent CAL. Twenty-six age-matched healthy children were enrolled as controls. PCR and gene sequencing were applied to explore the distribution of polymorphism of c.212-37insC (rs3832879) in FGF23 gene in KD patients and controls."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Among 40 children with KD, 14 (35%) carried the polymorphism of c.212-37insC (rs3832879) in FGF23 gene; among 26 controls, 6 (23%) carried such polymorphism. There was no significant difference in genotype distribution at this locus between the two groups (P=0.30). Among 16 children with CAL, 9 (56%) carried the polymorphism at this locus; among 24 children without CAL, 5 (21%) carried such polymorphism. As for the comparison of two subgroups with and without CAL, the difference in genotype distribution at this locus had statistical significance (P=0.02, OR=4.89, 95% CI: 1.21-19.71)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The polymorphism of c.212-37insC (rs3832879) in FGF23 gene may not be associated with the pathogenesis of childhood KD, but it may be associated with the development of CAL in children with KD."
        }
      ]},
